{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Where She Went"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le12ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Let's compare the simple past and present perfect:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span>  <br>It refers to an action that occurred at a definite time in the past.   <br><br>Examples:  <br>I said things that I didn't mean yesterday. <br>He caught me at a bad time last Saturday. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " These actions are finished when we have a definite time (yesterday, last Saturday).<br><br>  You can use other time expressions + simple past"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He did that ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in 2000<br>                                         last night<br>                                         last weekend<br>                                         on January 2nd<br>                                          three days ago\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span><br><br>It refers to an action that happened at an indefinite time in the past.<br><br>  Examples:  <br/>You guys have always made up and moved on.<br>  I have said terrible things.<br><br>  These actions can continue to the present."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have talked about getting married ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for years.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have been a couple ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since 2014.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have waited for Vanessa ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since she took off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never taken her suitcases.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you talk about routines in the past, you can use the expressions <span class=\"strong\">would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, followed by the verb in the basic form."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You used to talk about how you and her are going to get married. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You would always come over and blow off steam at place, right? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the expression <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> in the negative form, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span>. Look at the change in the expression:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You used to talk about how you two are going to get married I used to count on you.<br/> I didn't use to talk to anybody else.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> for the negative form of the expression:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We would talk about our future plans. <br/>We wouldn't spend time fighting at all.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to catch someone at a bad time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to interrupt someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did I catch you at a bad time?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about an argument."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mess it up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ruin something good or a good situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've really messed it up this time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to move on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop dealing with something or someone and do something else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You guys always made up and moved on."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cool off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to calm down"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You would always come to my house to cool off."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stupid"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "foolish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't believe how stupid I am! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be hard on yourself "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tell yourself negative things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't be so hard on yourself. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"},